{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The proof only needs the hypothesis instantiated with g = f. The resulting nonnegative self-inner-product has zero integral, hence is almost everywhere zero; continuity upgrades this to pointwise equality, and definiteness of the inner product yields f = 0. Reusing IsTestFunction.inner supplies both continuity and integrability with less elaboration.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  have h := hg f hf\\n  rw [integral_eq_zero_iff_of_nonneg] at h\\n  · rw [Continuous.ae_eq_iff_eq] at h\\n    · funext x\\n      simpa using congrFun h x\\n    · exact (hf.inner hf).smooth.continuous\\n    · exact continuous_const\\n  · exact fun x => real_inner_self_nonneg'\\n  · exact (hf.inner hf).integrable\"}"}}
